            <ArticleTitle>Restoring vaginal function in postmenopausal women with genitourinary syndrome of menopause.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>106-108</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/GME.0000000000000958</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Menopause practitioners are often asked to help postmenopausal women restore vaginal health and function. A common scenario is the postmenopausal woman who has been without a sexual partner for many years and is now about to resume or has already unsuccessfully attempted penetrative sexual activity. This Practice Pearl addresses the pathophysiology and effect of atrophic genital changes and offers advice on how vaginal health and comfortable sexual activity can be restored.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
